In case you did not see my post in the other thread, I had other
ideas. But, the phasing for invoking is intriguing and unique.

My first thought on the quest artifact for a Convict -- the Stash Bag.
A chaotic bag of holding which provides MR while in your inventory.
The bag can be used a weapon with the same skill as the ball and
chain. Invoke the bag and the bag generates gold or  jewels.
Most importantly as a Chaotic bag, you may not always get what you are
looking for. Depending on BUC status, the bag will not give you what
you thought you grabbed out of the bag; but some random item instead.
After providing a random item, inventory in the bag will not be
available for some random time period.
Carrying capacity for Burdened etc would all allow 25% more loot.
The Stash Bag cannot be placed inside another bag. The Stash Bag will
not allow stashing wands which will cause it's destruction "The Bag
resists your attempts to stash the wand inside" and flings the wand d3
away. The Stash Bag is of course waterproof.
As a Chaotic bag, this will limit other characters attempts to wish
for the Stash Bag.

